# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_uninstall_account_purge.py" "UNINSTALL ACCOUNT-WIDE PURGE GATE: PASS" "uninstall account-wide purge (privacy fix)" "uninstall account-wide purge (audit r4 privacy launch-blocker): the installation.deleted uninstall purge was 100% payload-driven -- it forgot ONLY the repos NAMED in the webhook's repositories array. GitHub OMITS that array for an 'All repositories' install (the common case), so an uninstall could leave a whole tenant's code graph + live claims in our DB = a broken 'we immediately purge on uninstall' privacy claim (the existing test_lifecycle_e2e always passed the repo back in the payload, so it never exercised the omitted-array path). The fix: (A) new core.purge_account_working_set_with_authority() forgets the pinned tenant's ENTIRE content-free working set (code_node/code_edge/graph_version/claim) across EVERY repo with no repo filter, retaining the append-only event ledger by design; (B) event_processor no longer fans installation.deleted out per-repo, so the uninstall falls through to the handler account-pinned and calls (A) regardless of the payload. Proven: a tenant with a working set across TWO repos + live claims is fully purged account-wide on uninstall (working set 0, ledger retained), the router no longer fans installation.deleted out per-repo while installation_repositories.removed still does (account survives, one repo named authoritatively). content-free" "uninstall account-wide purge: a tenant's ENTIRE code graph + live claims are forgotten on uninstall regardless of whether GitHub named the repos (the 'All repositories' omitted-array case), event ledger retained; the privacy claim now holds" 24
